Title: Text input on by default
Repository: love
Base: def245102c67909f9902095af613b1ae05249b62
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-20
Author: aros-loeve project
Problem: SDL3 sends no text events until SDL_StartTextInput is called, and this LOVE revision calls it only from love.keyboard.setTextInput. A game that relies on love.textinput without asking for it (the documented default on desktop systems) received key presses but no text.
Change: On AROS the window starts text input when it is set up. love.keyboard.setTextInput(false) still turns it off.
Scope: AROS (all targets)
Upstream: local-only
Verification: mainline x86_64 (nightly 2026-11-15), 2026-11-20: a test game that never calls setTextInput reports hasTextInput true and receives love.textinput for "a", "B" and "1"; before the change the same game received only keypressed.
Removal: when upstream starts text input by default on desktop systems, or has an AROS build
---
diff --git a/src/modules/window/sdl/Window.cpp b/src/modules/window/sdl/Window.cpp
index f3b09669c03a61fe47011921c5f0f61fb8a6b960..49899d3638ac51cf2cdaaaf0cb4cb32978fb4752 100644
--- a/src/modules/window/sdl/Window.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/window/sdl/Window.cpp
@@ -640,6 +640,12 @@ bool Window::setWindow(int width, int height, WindowSettings *settings)
 
 	SDL_RaiseWindow(window);
 
+#ifdef LOVE_AROS
+	// SDL3 sends no text events until text input is started. Games written
+	// for desktop systems expect love.textinput without asking for it.
+	SDL_StartTextInput(window);
+#endif
+
 	setVSync(f.vsync);
 
 	updateSettings(f, false);
